## Location
pkix-revocation/src/ocsp.rs:429-449 — fn hash_certid_input.

## Finding
```
fn hash_certid_input(oid: &der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier, data: &[u8]) -> crate::Result<HashOutput> {
    match *oid {
        OID_SHA1 => {
            use sha1::Digest as _;
            Ok(HashOutput::Sha1(sha1::Sha1::digest(data).into()))
        }
        OID_SHA256 => {
            use sha2::Digest as _;
            Ok(HashOutput::Sha256(sha2::Sha256::digest(data).into()))
        }
        OID_SHA384 => {
            use sha2::Digest as _;
            Ok(HashOutput::Sha384(sha2::Sha384::digest(data).into()))
        }
        OID_SHA512 => {
            use sha2::Digest as _;
            Ok(HashOutput::Sha512(sha2::Sha512::digest(data).into()))
        }
        _ => Err(Error::OcspMalformed),
    }
}
```

The Digest trait is a single trait imported from two crates. The use statements are duplicated across all four arms. Idiomatic Rust would hoist the imports to the top of the function:

```
fn hash_certid_input(oid: &der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier, data: &[u8]) -> crate::Result<HashOutput> {
    use sha1::Digest as _;
    use sha2::Digest as _;
    match *oid {
        OID_SHA1 => Ok(HashOutput::Sha1(sha1::Sha1::digest(data).into())),
        OID_SHA256 => Ok(HashOutput::Sha256(sha2::Sha256::digest(data).into())),
        OID_SHA384 => Ok(HashOutput::Sha384(sha2::Sha384::digest(data).into())),
        OID_SHA512 => Ok(HashOutput::Sha512(sha2::Sha512::digest(data).into())),
        _ => Err(Error::OcspMalformed),
    }
}
```

## Severity
P4 (opinion / cosmetic). This is purely stylistic — the per-arm imports work correctly because they bring the trait into scope just for that arm and the trait is used as '_' (anonymous). No correctness or perf difference.

## Possible justification for current form
A reader could argue per-arm imports make it clearer which sha* crate provides which Digest implementation. Counter-argument: 'use sha1::Digest as _' / 'use sha2::Digest as _' are imports of a *trait*, not an impl, so they are pure namespace decoration anyway.

## Recommendation
Hoist for readability. Low priority — the match body remains readable either way.
